WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.240
Have you ever had a nightmare that you’re
running down a long, dark hallway, getting

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.640
chased by something you can’t see?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.099
The thing behind you isn’t fast, but that
doesn’t matter.

00:00:10.099 --> 00:00:12.889
You can’t run forever, and the thing knows
it.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:15.419
It is a patient predator.

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:17.090
It toys with its food.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.860
At first, you move with speed and rhythm.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.009
The metallic scraping noise behind you grows
quieter.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:25.140
You run and stumble through the dark.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.029
Your muscles start to ache and your lungs
burn.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:29.189
Your pace slows.

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:30.980
It’s still coming.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.789
You can hear the scraping getting louder.

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:34.230
You start to panic.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.230
It’s completely dark.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.620
You don’t know where you’re running or
even what you’re running from.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:44.089
All you know - as you bump against the walls
and the sharp corners that rush towards you

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:46.850
- is that you can’t run forever.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:51.680
You trip, fall, and pain explodes through
your leg as your knee shatters on the concrete

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.680
ground.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.590
That scraping is getting louder.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.449
You can barely breathe.

00:00:56.449 --> 00:00:58.660
You can’t run anymore with your injury.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.340
There’s no way to stop what’s coming.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.769
There is no escape.

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:05.031
The scraping is right behind you.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.031
You scream.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:08.770
And then… you wake up.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.230
Your heart is pounding like thunder in your
chest and your sheets are soaked with sweat,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.340
but you’re safe.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.080
You’re out of those awful, dark hallways.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.729
But what if this wasn’t just a nightmare?

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:24.210
What if this scenario was real, and there
was no escape from the horror chasing you

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.210
in the darkness?

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:31.360
That’s what it’s like to have a close
encounter with SCP-1918, a sadistic, sentient

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.140
object that loves playing twisted games with
its prey.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:41.400
But this monster never plays fair, and even
worse, it’s always just a simple door away.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.430
It might even be hiding behind a door near
you, right now, waiting to start a game with

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.240
its new playmate.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.759
But soon you’ll understand why some doors
should never, ever be opened, and why some

00:01:54.759 --> 00:01:57.020
games are better left unplayed.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:03.369
x
SCP - 1918 is an anomaly with two parts: SCP-1918

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:09.610
itself, and SCP-1918-2, the monster’s underground
lair.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:16.300
The duo are a match made in hell, as the chambers
and hallways of 1918-2 are perfectly tailored

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.190
to 1918’s violent hobbies.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:24.600
Nobody knows how long this anomaly has been
operating, but it’s probably behind countless

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.270
disappearances.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:31.020
After all, 1918 has a habit of breaking its
toys...

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.880
The nightmare began in a small town in Maine,
with a population of only 226 people.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.480
But that population was about to get lower.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.310
People in the town began to report strange
noises at night, a droning, metal-on-concrete

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.190
scraping noise, like someone dragging a lead
pipe along the ground.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.760
At first, people just ignored the sound.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.730
It was all in their heads, or maybe just a
faulty oven or a washing machine on the fritz.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:01.650
Anything that would allow them to forget about
the noise and get on with their daily lives.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.370
But the noises were coming from below.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:09.900
They could be heard out on the streets, most
audibly near manholes and sewer grates.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.460
People started feeling unsafe in their homes.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.490
The noises were spooking animals and children.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.980
People were losing sleep.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.450
That scraping they all tried to ignore was
beginning to get to them all.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:26.110
Letters, emails, and angry phone calls to
the town council were piling up.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.140
Something had to be done before the whole
town went crazy with fear.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:34.080
The mayor authorized four utility workers
to investigate the source of the noise at

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.480
a local sewage treatment facility.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.530
Considering the scraping was loudest near
the sewer grates, everyone just assumed that

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.260
whatever was causing all this must be connected
to the sewers.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.960
Four utility workers were sent to investigate
the facility, only to find that the machinery

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.370
on site was working just fine.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:55.730
The source of the problems must have been
coming directly from the underground sewer-lines

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:56.900
themselves.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:01.150
The four workers, equipped with headlamps,
descended into a long service tunnel that

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.310
fed into the sewer system.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.260
As they passed deeper into the tunnel, the
darkness around them became thicker.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.600
It was a tangible presence that drowned out
the light of their headlamps, similar to the

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.540
anomalous phenomenon exhibited by SCP - 087.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:22.011
When the utility workers tried to turn back,
they discovered another impossibility: It

00:04:22.011 --> 00:04:26.870
seemed that the tunnel behind them had become
a solid concrete wall.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.630
They were trapped, but where?

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.410
It was too dark to tell.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.230
Confused and terrified, the four men stuck
together, attempting to find a way out.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:39.980
It was too dark to see their hand in front
of their face, so all they could do was navigate

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.910
slowly by feeling the walls around them.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.700
These walls felt oddly...crusty.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:51.500
There was a kind of faint, metallic stench
hanging in the air, too, like old blood.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.620
Something horrible had happened here, and
something horrible was about to happen again.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.900
All they could do was keep moving and try
to stay calm.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:05.180
Eventually, after hours of pawing at walls
in the dark, they found an open doorway.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:10.470
One by one, they filed inside, only to feel
blinded when bright, white ceiling lights

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.130
suddenly switched on.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:18.770
The room was all white, and filled with pipes,
large and small, running from wall to wall.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:22.950
Just then one of the utility workers let out
an ear-splitting scream and pointed towards

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:23.950
the doorway.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.460
His colleagues turned, and gasped in shock.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.870
There was something outside the door, and
it was staring at them.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.620
The object filled up almost the entire doorway.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:38.670
It seemed like a demonic hobby horse, made
from a black-and-white, candy-striped metal

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.690
pole with a crude plastic head on top.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:47.300
The head looked like a clown’s, with a wide,
toothy grin, but no visible eyes.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.220
It was SCP-1918.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:56.030
The utility workers were frozen as the object
leaned forward slightly, and slithered into

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:00.090
the room, the bottom of the metal pipe scraping
against the ground.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:05.570
It was the exact same scraping noise that’d
been haunting the concerned townsfolk up above.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.920
This was the thing behind it all.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:15.620
And as the object moved, its metal pole started
to scrape words into the ground: Tik Tak Tow

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.640
None of the four utility workers were ever
seen again.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:23.700
It didn’t take long for the SCP Foundation
to descend upon this quiet Maine town and

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.210
pick up the pieces.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:30.020
All relevant officials were provided amnestics,
and cover stories were created for the disappearances

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:32.190
of the four utility workers.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:36.120
The Foundation also commandeered the sewage
treatment facility that held the entrance

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:43.600
to SCP-1918-2, replacing all key roles at
the facility with undercover Foundation personnel.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:49.550
SCP-1918 was given a Euclid' classification
due to the fixed nature of its hunting grounds,

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.070
and then the real research began.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:55.760
The Foundation soon made some disturbing discoveries.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:00.970
Entrances into the SCP-1918-2 area didn’t
follow any kind of logic.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:07.180
The hunting ground of SCP-1918 can be entered
from almost any location, if you’re unlucky

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.180
enough.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:13.310
There are currently 9 known entrances, including
5 sewage grates, 3 utility shafts located

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.290
in a sewage facility, and 1 toilet.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.650
And these are just the ones the Foundation
knows about.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:27.110
There are a huge number of ways to enter SCP-1918-2,
but to this day, nothing has ever been able

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.460
to leave.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:34.080
SCP-1918-2 is contained twenty meters below
the streets of this unassuming Maine town.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:39.500
Personnel, aside from Foundation-approved
D-class guinea pigs. are refused entrance.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:45.210
Researchers have mapped out the layout of
1918-2 through seismic imaging of SCP-1918’s

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.730
movements.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:53.320
There are 18 identical room pairs in SCP-1918-2,
or 9 compound rooms.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:58.330
Rooms are differentiated between a '1' room
and a '2' room by crude carvings on the floors

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.970
outside of the individual rooms.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:07.030
SCP-1918-2 is symmetrical, with half a meter
wide paths circling each compound room.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:11.580
The only deviations to this construction are
the location of entrances on the sides of

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.410
each individual room, which vary randomly
while the location is “active.”

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:21.040
What exactly does SCP-1918 do in this private
little maze?

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.120
It plays games, of course.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.040
Its two favorites - as indicated by the words
it scrapes onto the ground - are “Tik Tak

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.199
Tow” and “Memoree”

00:08:31.199 --> 00:08:37.350
In Tik Tak Tow, 1918 moves to each “1”
room, leaving behind "X" markings on the floors

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:42.070
if the room is not already marked with an
"O" in a manner similar to a game of "Tic

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.070
Tac Toe''.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:48.010
How a victim is meant to accomplish making
a mark or understand this process is unknown,

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:50.000
as no aides are given.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.850
Blood is commonly used by victims to make
their markings, hence the rusty smell in many

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:55.980
of the rooms.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:01.620
In Memoree, the trapped victim is rendered
unconscious by blunt force, presumably from

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.470
SCP-1918.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:07.400
The subject regains consciousness in a random
section of the facility.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.500
Success is marked by finding a “1” room
identical to the central room.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:17.000
This event seems to possess a time limit,
as the subject is pursued by SCP-1918 throughout

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.870
the halls of the facility.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:23.220
The subject "wins'' by marking the correct
room with an "O".

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.310
What happens if you win or lose these games?

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:32.610
It’s important to note that SCP-1918 is
very competitive, and doesn’t play fair.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:37.290
If you win, the object will merely accuse
you of cheating, and start a new game.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:42.650
This will happen again and again, until eventually…
you lose.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:43.650
And when you do?

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:51.000
Well, take the horrifying encounter D-Class
personnel member D-2934 had with SCP-1918.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:58.630
Wearing video and audio equipment, D-2934
was led into SCP-1918-2 by Foundation researchers.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:03.649
When he eventually found his way to the central
room, 1918 challenged him to a game of Tik

00:10:03.649 --> 00:10:04.649
Tak Tow.

00:10:04.649 --> 00:10:09.390
And, against all odds, D-2934 won the game.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:12.210
But 1918 didn’t take kindly to that.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:17.620
It accused D-2934 of cheating, carving its
accusations into the ground before challenging

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.450
him to a deadly game of Memoree.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:25.670
After hours of chasing, D-2934 eventually
lost his mind and was backed into a corner

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:27.560
by 1918.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.861
As the object made its way towards him, he
panicked, ripped a pipe from the wall, and

00:10:31.861 --> 00:10:34.650
began smashing 1918’s head.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:38.839
As the plastic cracked under the force of
the blows, Foundation scientists could see

00:10:38.839 --> 00:10:40.700
real brains inside.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:44.460
D-2934 screamed, and the video feed cut off.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:49.880
When the video turned back on some time later,
1918 stared into the camera with a different

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.400
head mounted atop its metal pole.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:56.730
One that, just a few hours earlier, had belonged
to the unfortunate D-2934.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:03.080
If there’s one lesson to be learned from
this terrifying anomaly, it’s that there

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.960
truly is no escape from SCP-1918.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:15.440
Now go watch “SCP - 5031 - Yet Another Murder
Monster” and “SCP - 3999 - I Am At The

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.670
Center of Everything That Happens To Me”
for more unspeakable horrors from the Foundation

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.610
Archives!

